-- חוזר תנאי שירות תשס"א/1 — שיחות טלפון (אוקטובר 2000)
-- The director of conditions of service of teaching employees quotes the
-- monthly telephone-call quotas the annex to the February 1970 wage
-- agreement gave principals, deputy principals and teachers, and the
-- Accountant-General's circular converting such quotas into money amounts
-- from 1.4.2000.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT common

§ `שיחות טלפון`

-- akn:preamble/p1 akn:preamble/p2 akn:preamble/p3 akn:preamble/p4 The circular's number, its title, its date and the subject line; no rule.

@desc The posts the 1970 annex gives a call quota to.
DECLARE `teaching post` IS ONE OF
    `school principal`                 @desc "מנהל בי\"ס לכל רמותיו": a principal of a school of any level
    `deputy principal`                 @desc "סגן מנהל בי\"ס לכל רמותיו"
    `rank-and-file teaching employee`  @desc "עובד הוראה מן השורה למעט מנהל וסגן מנהל"

@desc A teaching employee, as far as this circular asks about them.
DECLARE `telephone case` HAS
    `post`                          IS A `teaching post`
    `share of a full position`      IS A NUMBER  @desc the share of one full position the employee holds (1 = one full position)
    `has a private telephone`       IS A BOOLEAN @desc the employee has a private telephone, the condition the quoted Accountant-General circular names

§§ `1–3 The quotas of the 1970 annex`

-- ¶¶1–3 as quoted from the annex to the wage agreement of February 1970
-- (preamble ¶5 introduces them): a quota of calls reimbursed each month,
-- "for one full position".
@ref akn:preamble/p5 akn:art_1 akn:art_2 akn:art_3
GIVEN p IS A `teaching post`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the monthly call quota for one full position` p IS
    CONSIDER p
    WHEN `school principal`                THEN 150
    WHEN `deputy principal`                THEN 125
    WHEN `rank-and-file teaching employee` THEN 50

§§ `4 The conversion into amounts`

@ref akn:art_4
`the conversion takes effect` MEANS Date 1 4 2000

-- The table AS PRINTED, in its order: the amount, and the quota it replaces.
-- The table names no currency or period; it replaces a monthly quota, so its
-- amounts are read as monthly amounts in shekels.
@ref akn:art_4/t1
DECLARE `conversion row` HAS
    `amount instead of the quota`  IS A NUMBER
    `quota the amount replaces`    IS A NUMBER

@ref akn:art_4/t1
`the conversion table` MEANS
    LIST `conversion row` 12.15 50,
         `conversion row` 29.13 125,
         `conversion row` 36.45 150,
         `conversion row` 42.53 175,
         `conversion row` 48.60 200

-- ¶4: from 1.4.2000 the payment no longer rests on a quota of calls; each
-- quota is converted to the amount the table sets beside it. A quota the
-- table does not print has no amount here.
@ref akn:art_4
GIVEN quota IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `the amount the table gives instead of a quota of` quota IS
    CONSIDER filter (GIVEN r YIELD r's `quota the amount replaces` EQUALS quota) `the conversion table`
    WHEN EMPTY                THEN NOTHING
    WHEN r FOLLOWED BY others THEN JUST (r's `amount instead of the quota`)

-- F-2000-10_tnai-sherut_tashsa_01_sichot-telefon-b: the circular quotes and
-- never says the conversion applies to teaching employees; the conversion
-- it quotes is stated for state employees with private telephones. The
-- reading adopted: from 1.4.2000 a teaching employee with a private
-- telephone is paid the amount the table sets beside the quota of their
-- post, and the condition of a private telephone carries over.
-- F-2000-10_tnai-sherut_tashsa_01_sichot-telefon-c: the quotas are "for one
-- full position" and the circular does not say what another share gets.
-- The reading adopted: the amount for one full position, pro-rated to the
-- share held, never above one position.
-- F-2000-10_tnai-sherut_tashsa_01_sichot-telefon-a: the amount for a
-- deputy principal is the printed 29.13.
@export default The monthly telephone amount (in shekels) a teaching employee is paid in place of a call quota, on the readings this file adopts
@ref akn:art_4
GIVEN c     IS A `telephone case` @desc the teaching employee
      `day` IS A DATE             @desc a day in the month the amount is for
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `the monthly telephone amount` c `day` IS
    IF `day` LESS THAN `the conversion takes effect` OR (NOT c's `has a private telephone`)
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE CONSIDER `the amount the table gives instead of a quota of` (`the monthly call quota for one full position` (c's `post`))
         WHEN JUST full THEN JUST (full TIMES min (c's `share of a full position`) 1)
         WHEN NOTHING   THEN NOTHING

DECLARE `telephone action` IS ONE OF
    `pay the telephone amount` HAS `telephone amount paid` IS A NUMBER

-- On F-…-b's reading, the employer pays the converted amount for each
-- month from 1.4.2000. The circular sets no payment date; time is counted in
-- months from the start of the month the amount is for.
@ref akn:art_4
GIVEN c     IS A `telephone case`
      `day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `telephone action`
DECIDE `the employer pays the telephone amount` c `day` IS
    CONSIDER `the monthly telephone amount` c `day`
    WHEN JUST due THEN
        PARTY `the employer`
        MUST  `pay the telephone amount` paid
              PROVIDED paid AT LEAST due
        WITHIN 1
        LEST  BREACH BY `the employer` BECAUSE "the telephone amount that replaced the call quota was not paid for the month"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FULFILLED

-- akn:conclusions The sign-off of the director of conditions of service of teaching employees; no rule.

§§ `Findings`

-- F-2000-10_tnai-sherut_tashsa_01_sichot-telefon-a: four of the table's
-- five rows convert at one rate, the 50-call row's 12.15 / 50 = 0.243 a
-- call, to the agora (150 → 36.45, 175 → 42.525 ≈ 42.53, 200 → 48.60); the
-- 125-call row prints 29.13 where that rate gives 30.375.
`the rate a call the 50-call row sets` MEANS 12.15 DIVIDED BY 50

GIVEN r IS A `conversion row`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the row converts at that rate to the agora` r IF
        r's `amount instead of the quota` AT LEAST (r's `quota the amount replaces` TIMES `the rate a call the 50-call row sets`) MINUS 0.005
    AND r's `amount instead of the quota` AT MOST (r's `quota the amount replaces` TIMES `the rate a call the 50-call row sets`) PLUS 0.005

`the 125-call row alone departs from the rate the other rows share` MEANS
        all (GIVEN r YIELD r's `quota the amount replaces` EQUALS 125 OR `the row converts at that rate to the agora` r)
            `the conversion table`
    AND (NOT any (GIVEN r YIELD r's `quota the amount replaces` EQUALS 125 AND `the row converts at that rate to the agora` r)
                 `the conversion table`)
    AND `the amount the table gives instead of a quota of` 125 EQUALS JUST 29.13
    AND (125 TIMES `the rate a call the 50-call row sets`) MINUS 29.13 GREATER THAN 1
#ASSERT `the 125-call row alone departs from the rate the other rows share`

-- F-2000-10_tnai-sherut_tashsa_01_sichot-telefon-b: every numbered
-- paragraph is a quotation — ¶¶1–3 from the 1970 annex, ¶4 from the
-- Accountant-General's circular — and the circular adds no sentence of its
-- own; the conversion is stated for "עובדי מדינה בעלי טלפוניים פרטיים".
DECLARE `paragraph source` IS ONE OF
    `the annex to the February 1970 wage agreement`
    `the senior deputy Accountant-General's circular`
    `the circular itself`

`the source of each numbered paragraph` MEANS
    LIST `the annex to the February 1970 wage agreement`,
         `the annex to the February 1970 wage agreement`,
         `the annex to the February 1970 wage agreement`,
         `the senior deputy Accountant-General's circular`

`the circular quotes and never applies the conversion to teaching employees` MEANS
    all (GIVEN s YIELD NOT s EQUALS `the circular itself`) `the source of each numbered paragraph`
#ASSERT `the circular quotes and never applies the conversion to teaching employees`

-- F-2000-10_tnai-sherut_tashsa_01_sichot-telefon-c: a teacher on half a
-- position, pro-rated, has a quota of 25 calls, which no row converts; and
-- a principal above one position has a quota the words "למשרה מלאה אחת" do
-- not size.
`the table has no row for a half-position teacher's quota` MEANS
    `the amount the table gives instead of a quota of` (`the monthly call quota for one full position` `rank-and-file teaching employee` TIMES 0.5)
    EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the table has no row for a half-position teacher's quota`

§§ `Examples`

`a principal on a full position` MEANS
    `telephone case` WITH
        `post`                     IS `school principal`
        `share of a full position` IS 1
        `has a private telephone`  IS TRUE

`a deputy principal on a full position` MEANS
    `telephone case` WITH
        `post`                     IS `deputy principal`
        `share of a full position` IS 1
        `has a private telephone`  IS TRUE

`a teacher on half a position` MEANS
    `telephone case` WITH
        `post`                     IS `rank-and-file teaching employee`
        `share of a full position` IS 0.5
        `has a private telephone`  IS TRUE

`a teacher without a private telephone` MEANS
    `telephone case` WITH
        `post`                     IS `rank-and-file teaching employee`
        `share of a full position` IS 1
        `has a private telephone`  IS FALSE

-- The table reproduced for each post's quota.
#ASSERT `the monthly telephone amount` `a principal on a full position` (Date 1 5 2000) EQUALS JUST 36.45
#ASSERT `the monthly telephone amount` `a deputy principal on a full position` (Date 1 5 2000) EQUALS JUST 29.13
#ASSERT `the monthly telephone amount` `a teacher on half a position` (Date 1 5 2000) EQUALS JUST 6.075
#ASSERT `the monthly telephone amount` `a principal on a full position` (Date 31 3 2000) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the monthly telephone amount` `a teacher without a private telephone` (Date 1 5 2000) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the amount the table gives instead of a quota of` 175 EQUALS JUST 42.53
#ASSERT `the amount the table gives instead of a quota of` 100 EQUALS NOTHING

#TRACE `the employer pays the telephone amount` `a principal on a full position` (Date 1 5 2000) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the employer` DOES `pay the telephone amount` 36.45 AT 0
#TRACE `the employer pays the telephone amount` `a principal on a full position` (Date 1 5 2000) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the employer` DOES `pay the telephone amount` 12.15 AT 0
